<section class="tc-kv" aria-label="Key Visual"><header class="tc-head tc-head--center"><div><p class="tc-eyebrow" data-tc-enter>Key Visual</p><h2 data-tc-enter>A Seoul identity<br />on a global framework</h2></div><p class="tc-desc" data-tc-enter>Converge World Tour travels across cities, and every stop shares the same graphic system. We kept the global structure—navy ground, converge symbol and photo grid—and placed Gwanghwamun where the host city's landmark sits, giving the Korean event its own identity. The remaining grid cells show last year's Seoul event, so first-time invitees can sense its scale and atmosphere in advance.</p></header>
